  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following integral of a vector-valued function. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{4}\u27e82{t}^{2}-t,\\,3{e}^{-t}\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t=\u27e8$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\u27e82{t}^{2}-t,\\,3{e}^{-t}\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8{\\int }_{0}^{4}(2{t}^{2}-t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{4}3{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first component,\n\n$$\n\\int (2{t}^{2}-t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFor the second component,\n\n$$\n\\int 3{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=3\\cdot (-{e}^{-t})=-3{e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\u27e82{t}^{2}-t,\\,3{e}^{-t}\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8(\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{4},\\,(-3{e}^{-t}){|}_{0}^{4}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(\\frac{2}{3}(64)-\\frac{1}{2}(16))-0,\\,(-3{e}^{-4})-(-3)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(\\frac{128}{3}-8),\\,3(1-{e}^{-4})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{104}{3},\\,3(1-{e}^{-4})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{104}{3},\\,3(1-{e}^{-4})\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
